41. The prosecution has also produced a coherent and consistent following evidences :-
(i) testimony by the supposed signatories that they had not signed or forwarded the implicated documents;
FIR No. 373/2015 St. Vs. Kavita Mathur (ii) contemporaneous DD entries and rukka/tehrir which record objections and observations at the time;
(iii) the CFSL report identifying the questioned signatures as non-genuine;
(iv) court record entries showing filing of documents bearing those signatures;
and (v) the accused's conduct, including the alleged act of tearing the contested page and the sending of the intimidating message.
42.
